## Blinded Causal Plan

The full protocol is embedded in V1.3. Its first executable design, if separately authorized later, is:

| Arm | DHM uL | DEP uL | Evernyl nominal 20% uL | Raw total |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| D160 | 160 | 1,075 | 25 | 6,000 |
| D200 | 200 | 1,035 | 25 | 6,000 |
| D240 | 240 | 995 | 25 | 6,000 |
| D280 | 280 | 955 | 25 | 6,000 |
| D340-L | 340 | 895 | 25 | 6,000 |

D340-L is the stock-corrected legacy-DHM boundary, not the raw V1.2 recipe. D200 advances only if it preserves sport movement while improving lavender/wood legibility, comfort, fatigue, and re-smell desire against the neighboring arms in two independent blinded blocks. A D160/D200 tie selects D160.

After DHM localization, test 25 uL Evernyl 20% versus 25 uL DPG at constant total, then the Javanol 0/10/20-uL stock ladder, then zero versus one Romandolide. Exact stock basis and safety authority must be resolved before physical execution.

## Claim and Authorization Ceiling

- **Established:** exact file arithmetic, version lineage, current inventory representation, nominal active conservation, parser-compatible 10-uL floor, and governed model output.
- **HOLD:** Evernyl exact concentration basis, exact w/w ppm, material-specific safety, Ambrofix/Coumarin/Javanol stock details, composite-natural applicability, and release governance.
- **NOT TESTED:** smell, sport identity, lavender leadership, pleasure, re-smell desire, depth, luxury, recurrence, diffusion, longevity, Thai-local preference, heat behavior, stability, and superiority to V1.2.
- **NOT AUTHORIZED:** procurement, stock preparation, physical compounding, skin/blotter evaluation, recruitment, consumer testing, or release.

**Final status: THEORY ONLY / NOT TESTED / NO STOCK PREPARATION OR COMPOUNDING AUTHORIZED.**
